(Bugs #126/#127: the fix that refuses a malformed precision after a width
 must leave a width composed with a bare base letter alone - `{n:8x}` has
 no dot at all, so it never enters the precision boundary the fix moves,
 and keeps rendering the digits in hex, padded to width.)

a number called n is 255.
Print "[{n:8x}]".
Print "[{n:8}]".
